{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> Dry stubble. קש is a participle, and 'tongue of fire' [לשון אש] is an active participle." "<b>And like decayed stubble</b> — like קש, and like it תהרו חשש (Isaiah 33:11)." "And it lacks a bet before <b>להבה</b>, like כי ששת ימים (Exodus 20:11), הנמצא בית יי' (II Kings 18:15). For ירפה [if it is joined back] to חשש, it is an active participle [standing]." "<b>Like decay.</b> The root [נרקש] will decay, and it will not stand." "<b>Like dust.</b> Construct state, and it lacks ארץ or the like, so the meaning is: their fathers and their sons."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:02.296641878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}